# Topic taxonomy for the classifier.
#
# Copy this file to `topics.yaml` and adapt it to your own categories.
# `topics.yaml` is git-ignored so your personal taxonomy stays local.
#
# Each topic needs a `name` (the exact value used as the Gmail label and in
# the model output) and an optional `rule` describing when it applies.

# Cross-cutting guidance shown before the per-topic rules (optional).
guidance: |-
  - Choose the single most specific topic that fits the email.
  - Do NOT add a general parent or related category.

topics:
  - name: Work
    rule: Work-related correspondence from colleagues or clients.
  - name: Personal
    rule: Messages from friends and family.
  - name: Finance
    rule: Invoices, receipts, banking and payment notifications.
  - name: Newsletters
    rule: Recurring or mass informational mail.
  - name: Other
    rule: The final fallback.
